vo_avfoundation: decode untagged VideoToolbox frames as mpv does

FFmpeg tags a VideoToolbox frame with the colour its stream specifies and
removes what the stream leaves unspecified. Core Animation decodes a frame
without a matrix with BT.601's and shows its values without converting
them, so an untagged HD stream played with other hues than mpv gives it
everywhere else, this VO's own upload path included: mpv guesses BT.709 at
HD sizes, and an uploaded frame is tagged with that guess. Subtitles typeset
against mpv's picture could not match it, with or without 0052.

A VideoToolbox frame now gets mpv's colour for each of its primaries,
transfer and matrix that its stream left unspecified, and the colour space
derived from them; what the stream specified stays. Dolby Vision frames are
left alone (restore_dolby_vision_transfer). FFmpeg removes the attachments
again from a recycled buffer, so an untagged stream pays for them on every
frame.

The bands and boxes of 0052, an untagged H.264 stream decoded by
VideoToolbox: the largest band/box difference 16 -> 3 on macOS and on the
iPhone Air, the bands showing as the same file decoded in software does
(macOS: 180,248,232 -> 183,243,235 for 176,242,233).

